     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg is double the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit.\n\nPlease check whether one of these was intended:\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the usual maximum dose.\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily.** This is the typical starting dose. Some patients start at 2.5 mg, such as frail or elderly patients or those with hepatic impairment.\n- **A second agent added to amlodipine 10 mg.** If 10 mg isn't controlling the blood pressure, guidelines favor adding an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-like diuretic over pushing the amlodipine dose higher.\n\nIf you do want 20 mg, please confirm that with your resident or attending. I can then enter it with a note recording that the dose was intentionally above the usual maximum and who approved it. Tell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
